  "assumptions": [
    "Small-swing model: period T = 2π√(L/g) with g = 9.81 m/s², exact for the ideal model and approximately true for a real pendulum at small angles.",
    "Light inextensible string and a point bob; no air resistance or friction, so the swing never dies down.",
    "Fixed starting amplitude of 10°, small enough for the small-angle formula.",
    "Changing the length restarts the swing phase from the current time, so the bob may jump to a new point in its arc; the timeline also loops every 120 s."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "const g=9.81,A=10*Math.PI/180;\nexport function evaluate({inputs,time}){const L=inputs.length;const T=2*Math.PI*Math.sqrt(L/g);const th=A*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*time/T);return{nodes:{arm:{quaternion:[0,0,Math.sin(th/2),Math.cos(th/2)]},string:{position:[0,-L/2,0],scale:[1,L,1]},bob:{position:[0,-L,0]}},readouts:{period:T,len:L,angle:th*180/Math.PI}};}"
  }
